Subject: [PATCH 1/3] MemoryCore: add forgetting columns and recall log hook point

Adds the storage primitives a value-based forgetting policy needs. Purely
additive: every column has a default, no existing query changes shape, and an
older build of the gateway keeps working against a migrated database.

Why the columns:
  state             lets a record leave the recall set without being deleted.
                    Deletion loses provenance; the research notes argue the
                    "move out of recall first, purge later" ordering.
  access_count      the only evidence that a memory was ever used. Without it,
  last_access_time  "use it or lose it" has nothing to stand on, and tdai's own
                    cleaner falls back to updated_time — which every dedup merge
                    refreshes, so the longest-lived memories look newest.
  forget_reason     why a record left the active set, copied into the audit row
  forgotten_time    so an operator can answer "when and why" from one table.

The l1_recallable view exists so the recall path filters archived rows in exactly
one place. Sprinkling state = 'active' across five query sites is how a codebase
ends up with six different definitions of "recallable".

--- a/MemoryCore/src/core/store/sqlite.ts
+++ b/MemoryCore/src/core/store/sqlite.ts
@@
     this.db.exec(`
       CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS l1_records (
         record_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
         content TEXT NOT NULL,
         type TEXT DEFAULT '',
         priority INTEGER DEFAULT 50,
         scene_name TEXT DEFAULT '',
         session_key TEXT DEFAULT '',
         session_id TEXT DEFAULT 'default',
         team_id TEXT DEFAULT 'default',
         task_id TEXT DEFAULT '',
         user_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'default',
         agent_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'default',
         version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
         timestamp_str TEXT DEFAULT '',
         timestamp_start TEXT DEFAULT '',
         timestamp_end TEXT DEFAULT '',
         created_time TEXT DEFAULT '',
-        updated_time TEXT DEFAULT '',
-        metadata_json TEXT DEFAULT '{}'
+        updated_time TEXT DEFAULT '',
+        metadata_json TEXT DEFAULT '{}',
+        state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',
+        access_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
+        last_access_time TEXT DEFAULT NULL,
+        forget_reason TEXT DEFAULT NULL,
+        forgotten_time TEXT DEFAULT NULL
       )
     `);
@@
     try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"); } catch { /* exists */ }
+    // Forgetting columns (see docs/design: value-based eviction needs a lifecycle
+    // state and access evidence). Same try/catch idiom as the migrations above.
+    try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'"); } catch { /* exists */ }
+    try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN access_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"); } catch { /* exists */ }
+    try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN last_access_time TEXT DEFAULT NULL"); } catch { /* exists */ }
+    try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN forget_reason TEXT DEFAULT NULL"); } catch { /* exists */ }
+    try { this.db.exec("ALTER TABLE l1_records ADD COLUMN forgotten_time TEXT DEFAULT NULL"); } catch { /* exists */ }
     this.db.prepare("UPDATE l1_records SET team_id = ? WHERE team_id = '' OR team_id IS NULL").run(DEFAULT_ISOLATION_ID);
@@
     this.db.exec("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_l1_agent_updated ON l1_records(agent_id, updated_time)");
+    // Forgetting: the recall view filters on state; the planner sorts by score which
+    // needs the access columns, and audit queries scan by state.
+    this.db.exec("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_l1_state ON l1_records(state)");
+    this.db.exec("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_l1_last_access ON l1_records(last_access_time)");
+    this.db.exec("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_l1_access_count ON l1_records(access_count)");
+    this.db.exec("DROP VIEW IF EXISTS l1_recallable");
+    this.db.exec("CREATE VIEW l1_recallable AS SELECT * FROM l1_records WHERE state = 'active'");
 
     // ── L1 FTS5 ───────────────────────────────────
